#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><title>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to Use This Book"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:164
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      In addition to expository text, this book has a few features designed to encourage you to interact with the mathematics.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><title>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "<em>Investigate!</em> questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:172
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Sprinkled throughout the sections (usually at the very beginning of a topic) you will find open-ended questions designed to engage you with the topic soon to be discussed.\n"
"        You really should spend some time thinking about, or even working through, these problems before reading the section.  However, don't worry if you cannot find a satisfying solution right away.  The goal is to pique your interest, so you will read what is next looking for answers.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><title>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preview Activities"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:180
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Most sections include a structured preview activity.  These contain leading questions that you should be able to completely answer before reading the section.  The idea is that the questions prime you to engage meaningfully with the new content ahead.  If you are using the online version, most of these questions will provide you with immediate feedback so you can be confident moving forward.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><title>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:184 source/sec_seq-induction.ptx:518
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        I have tried to include the <q>correct</q> number of examples.\n"
"        For those examples that include <em>problems</em>, full solutions are included.\n"
"        Before reading the solution, try to at least have an understanding of what the problem is asking.\n"
"        Unlike some textbooks, the examples are not meant to be all-inclusive for problems you will see in the exercises.\n"
"        They should not be used as a blueprint for solving other problems.\n"
"        Instead, use the examples to deepen your understanding of the concepts and techniques discussed in each section.\n"
"        Then use this understanding to solve the exercises at the end of each section.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><title>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:199
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:202
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        You get good at math through practice.\n"
"        Each section concludes with practice problems meant to solidify concepts and basic skills presented in that section; the online version provides immediate feedback on these problems.  There are then additional exercises that are more challenging and open-ended.  These might be assigned as written homework or used in class as group work.  Some of the additional exercises have hints or solutions in the back of the book, but use these as little as possible.  Struggle is good for you.  \n"
"        At the end of each chapter, a larger collection of similar exercises is included (as a sort of <q>chapter review</q>) which might bridge the material of different sections in that chapter.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><title>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:210
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interactive Online Version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:213
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        For those of you reading this in print or as a PDF, I encourage you to also check out the interactive online version.  Many of the preview activities and exercises are interactive and can give you immediate feedback.  Some of these have randomized components, allowing you to practice many similar versions of the same problems until you master the topic.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:217
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Hints and solutions to examples are also hidden away behind an extra click to encourage you to think about the problem before reading the solution.  There is a good search feature available as well, and the index has expandable links to see the content without jumping to the page immediately.  There is also a python scratch pad (the pencil icon) so you can try out some code if you feel so inclined.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:221
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Additional interactivity is planned.\n"
"        These <q>bonus</q> features will be added on a rolling basis, so keep an eye out!\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <frontmatter><preface><paragraphs><p>
#: source/frontmatter.ptx:226
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        You can view the interactive version for free at <url po4a-id=0> or by scanning the QR code below.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

