"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><introduction><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Let <m>P(x)</m> be the predicate, <q><m>17x + 1</m> is even.</q>\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><statement><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:154
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:207
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          Is <m>P(15)</m> true or false?\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><solution><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:159
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          <m>P(15)</m> is true, since <m>17 \\cdot 15 + 1 = 256</m> is even.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><statement><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:166
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:219
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          What, if anything, can you conclude about <m>\\exists x P(x)</m> from the truth value of <m>P(15)</m>?\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><solution><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:171
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          Since <m>P(15)</m> is true, we know that <m>\\exists x P(x)</m> is true.  There is at least one <m>x</m> for which <m>P(x)</m> is true.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><statement><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:178
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          What, if anything, can you conclude about <m>\\forall x P(x)</m> from the truth value of <m>P(15)</m>?\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><solution><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:183
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          Just because one value of <m>x</m> makes <m>P(x)</m> true does not mean that all values of <m>x</m> make <m>P(x)</m> true.  But it could be.  So we cannot conclude that <m>\\forall x P(x)</m> is true or false.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><introduction><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:201
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Let <m>P(x)</m> be the predicate, <q><m>18x + 1</m> is even.</q>\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><solution><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:212
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          <m>P(15)</m> is false, since <m>18 \\cdot 15 + 1 = 271 </m> is odd.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><solution><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:224
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          Since <m>P(15)</m> is false, we do not know whether <m>\\exists x P(x)</m> is true.  There could be some other value of <m>x</m> for which <m>P(x)</m> is true.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><task><solution><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:236
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          We know that there is some value of <m>x</m> makes <m>P(x)</m> false so we know that <m>\\forall x P(x)</m> is false.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/practice/logic-statements.ptx:247
