#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:144
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\tDoes this truth table make sense?  Should we believe it?  Look in particular at the third row: F, T, T, and consider the implication, <q>If <m>5 \\lt 3</m> then <m>5+3 = 8</m>.</q>  Does that statement <em>\n"
"\t\tfeel</em> true?  The truth table says it should be (since <m>5 \\lt 3</m> is false, and <m>5+3 = 8</m> is true).\n"
"\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:149
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\tMuch of what we will do in the remainder of this section is convince ourselves that this truth table makes sense.  \n"
"\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:163
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\tConsider the statement, <q>If Tommy doesn't eat his broccoli, then he will not get any ice cream.</q>  Which of the following statements mean the same thing (i.e., will be true in the same situations)?  Select all that apply.\n"
"\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:170
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIf Tommy does eat his broccoli, then he will get ice cream.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><feedback><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:175
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAre you sure?  Did we say what happens when he <em>does</em> eat the broccoli, or only what happens when he doesn't?\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIf Tommy gets ice cream, then he ate his broccoli.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><feedback><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIf he got ice cream, he must have eaten the broccoli, because if he didn't, then he wouldn't have had ice cream.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIf Tommy doesn't get ice cream, then he didn't eat his broccoli.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><feedback><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:199
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCould there have been a reason that Tommy doesn't get ice cream even if he did eat his broccoli?\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:206
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTommy ate his broccoli and still didn't get any ice cream.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><feedback><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:211
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThis is the opposite of the original statement (it is false precisely when the original statement is true).\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:221
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tSuppose that your shady uncle offers you the following deal: If you loan him your car, then he will bring you tacos.\n"
"\t\t\t\tIn which of the following situations would it be fair to say that your uncle is a liar (i.e., that his statement was false)?  Select all that apply.\n"
"\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:229
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tYou loan him your car.\n"
"\t\t\t\tHe brings you tacos.\n"
"\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:237
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tYou loan him your car.\n"
"\t\t\t\tHe never buys you tacos.\n"
"\t\t\t"
