#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:252
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tMaybe he just really likes giving you tacos.\n"
"\t\t\t\tThat's not enough to say he was a liar, is it?\n"
"\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:260
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tYou don't loan him your car.\n"
"\t\t\t\tHe never brings you tacos.\n"
"\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:271
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tConsider the <em>sentence</em>, <q>If <m>x \\ge 10</m>, then <m>x^2 \\ge 25</m>.</q>  This sentence becomes a statement when we replace <m>x</m> by a value, or <q>capture</q> the <m>x</m> in the scope of a quantifier.  Which of the following claims are true (select all that apply)?\n"
"\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:278
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\tIf we replace <m>x</m> by <m>15</m>, then the resulting statement is true.  (Note, <m>15^2 = 225</m>.)\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:285
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\tIf we replace <m>x</m> by <m>3</m>, then the resulting statement is true.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:292
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIf we replace <m>x</m> by <m>6</m>, then the resulting statement is true.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:299
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThe universal generalization (<q>for all <m>x</m>, if <m>x \\ge 10</m> the <m>x^2 \\ge 25</m></q>) is true.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:306
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThere is a number we could replace <m>x</m> with that makes the statement false.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:316
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tConsider the statement, <q>If I see a movie, then I eat popcorn</q> (which happens to be true).\n"
"\t\t\t\tBased solely on your intuition of English, which of the following statements mean the same thing?  Select all that apply.\n"
"\t\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><worksheet><exercise><choices><choice><statement><p>
#: source/sec_logic-implications.ptx:324
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\t\t\tIf I eat popcorn, then I see a movie.\n"
"\t\t\t"
