#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-proofs.ptx:590
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Your <q>friend</q> has shown you a <q>proof</q>\n"
"        he wrote to show that <m>1 = 3</m>.\n"
"        Here is the proof:\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><proof><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-proofs.ptx:597
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          I claim that <m>1 = 3</m>.\n"
"          Of course we can do anything to one side of an equation as long as we also do it to the other side.\n"
"          So subtract 2 from both sides.\n"
"          This gives <m>-1 = 1</m>.\n"
"          Now square both sides, to get <m>1 = 1</m>.\n"
"          And we all agree this is true.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-proofs.ptx:607
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        What is going on here?\n"
"        Is your friend's argument valid?\n"
"        Is the argument a proof of the claim <m>1=3</m>?\n"
"        Carefully explain using what we know about logic.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><hint><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-proofs.ptx:615
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Your friend's proof is a proof, but of what?  What implication follows from the given proof?  Is that helpful?  \n"
"      "
