#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:542
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Explain what the statement says in words.\n"
"              Is this statement true?\n"
"              Be sure to state what you are taking the universe of discourse to be.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:550
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Write the converse of the statement,\n"
"              both in words and in symbols.\n"
"              Is the converse true?\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:558
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Write the contrapositive of the statement,\n"
"              both in words and in symbols.\n"
"              Is the contrapositive true?\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:566
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Write the negation of the statement,\n"
"              both in words and in symbols.\n"
"              Is the negation true?\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:579
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              For any number <m>x</m>,\n"
"              if it is the case that adding any number to <m>x</m> gives that number back,\n"
"              then multiplying any number by <m>x</m> will give 0.\n"
"              This is true\n"
"              (of the integers or the reals).\n"
"              The <q>if</q> part only holds if <m>x = 0</m>,\n"
"              and in that case, anything times <m>x</m> will be 0.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:591
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              The converse in words is this:\n"
"              For any number <m>x</m>,\n"
"              if everything times <m>x</m> is zero,\n"
"              then everything added to <m>x</m> gives itself.\n"
"              Or in symbols:\n"
"              <m>\\forall x (\\forall z (x \\cdot z = 0) \\imp \\forall y (x + y = y))</m>.\n"
"              The converse is true:\n"
"              The only number which when multiplied by any other number gives 0 is <m>x = 0</m>.\n"
"              And if <m>x = 0</m>, then <m>x + y = y</m>.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:605
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              The contrapositive in words is:\n"
"              For any number <m>x</m>,\n"
"              if there is some number which when multiplied by <m>x</m> does not give zero,\n"
"              then there is some number which when added to <m>x</m> does not give that number.\n"
"              In symbols: <m>\\forall x (\\exists z (x\\cdot z \\ne 0) \\imp \\exists y (x + y \\ne y))</m>.\n"
"              We know the contrapositive must be true because the original implication is true.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:616
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              The negation:\n"
"              There is a number <m>x</m> such that any number added to <m>x</m> gives the number back again,\n"
"              but there is a number you can multiply <m>x</m> by and not get 0.\n"
"              In symbols: <m>\\exists x (\\forall y (x + y = y) \\wedge \\exists z (x \\cdot z \\ne 0))</m>.\n"
"              Of course since the original implication is true, the negation is false.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:633
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Simplify the following.\n"
"\n"
"        "
