"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:664
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Consider the statement, <q>For all integers <m>n</m>,\n"
"        if <m>n</m> is odd, then <m>7n</m> is odd.</q>\n"
"\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:677
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Prove the converse.\n"
"              What sort of proof are you using?\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p><proof><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:693
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                  Let <m>n</m> be an integer.\n"
"                  Assume <m>n</m> is odd.\n"
"                  So <m>n = 2k+1</m> for some integer <m>k</m>.\n"
"                  Then\n"
"                  "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p><proof><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:699
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
".\n"
"                "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p><proof><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:703
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                  Since <m>7k + 3</m> is an integer,\n"
"                  we see that <m>7n</m> is odd.\n"
"                "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:713
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              The converse is: For all integers <m>n</m>,\n"
"              if <m>7n</m> is odd, then <m>n</m> is odd.\n"
"              We will prove this by contrapositive.\n"
"\n"
"              "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p><proof><p>
#: source/exercises/logic-conc.ptx:719
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                  Let <m>n</m> be an integer.\n"
"                  Assume <m>n</m> is not odd.\n"
"                  Then <m>n = 2k</m> for some integer <m>k</m>.\n"
"                  So <m>7n = 14k = 2(7k)</m> which is to say <m>7n</m> is even.\n"
"                  Therefore <m>7n</m> is not odd.\n"
"                "
msgstr ""

