#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      Unless it is already a tree, a given graph <m>G</m> will have multiple spanning trees.\n"
"      How similar or different must these be?\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/gt-trees.ptx:405
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Must all spanning trees of a given graph be isomorphic to each other? Explain why or give a counterexample.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/gt-trees.ptx:411
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Must all spanning trees of a given graph have the same number of edges? Explain why or give a counterexample.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/gt-trees.ptx:417
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Must all spanning trees of a graph have the same number of leaves (vertices of degree 1)? Explain why or give a counterexample.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/gt-trees.ptx:429
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            No, although there are graphs for which this is true.\n"
"            For example, <m>K_4</m> has a spanning tree that is a path (of three edges) and also a spanning tree that is a star (with center vertex of degree 3).\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/gt-trees.ptx:436
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Yes.\n"
"            For a fixed graph, we have a fixed number <m>v</m> of vertices.\n"
"            Any spanning tree of the graph will also have <m>v</m> vertices, and since it is a tree, must have <m>v-1</m> edges.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/gt-trees.ptx:444
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            No, although there are graphs for which this is true (note that if all spanning trees are isomorphic, then all spanning trees will have the same number of leaves).\n"
"            Again, <m>K_4</m> is a counterexample.\n"
"            One spanning tree is a path, with only two leaves, and another spanning tree is a star with 3 leaves.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

