#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><investigation><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        When a connected graph can be drawn without any edges crossing,\n"
"        it is called <term>planar</term>.\n"
"        When a planar graph is drawn in this way,\n"
"        it divides the plane into regions called <term>faces</term>.\n"
"\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><investigation><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Draw, if possible,\n"
"              two different planar graphs with the same number of vertices, edges,\n"
"              and faces.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><investigation><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Draw, if possible,\n"
"              two different planar graphs with the same number of vertices and edges,\n"
"              but a different number of faces.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      When is it possible to draw a graph so that none of the edges cross?\n"
"      If this <em>is</em> possible,\n"
"      we say the graph is <term>planar</term>\n"
"      (since you can draw it on the <em>plane</em>).\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:71
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      Notice that the definition of planar includes the phrase\n"
"      <q>it is possible to.</q>\n"
"      This means that even if a graph does not look like it is planar,\n"
"      it still might be.\n"
"      Perhaps you can redraw it in a way in which no edges cross.\n"
"      For example, this is a planar graph:\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><image><description>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          A drawing of K2,3 with two vertices in a top row, each adjacent to each of the three vertices on the bottom row.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:113
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      That is because we can redraw it like this:\n"
"    "
