#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:140
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      When a planar graph is drawn without edges crossing,\n"
"      the edges and vertices of the graph divide the plane into regions.\n"
"      We will call each region a <term>face</term>.\n"
"      The graph above has 3 faces\n"
"      (yes, we <em>do</em> include the\n"
"      <q>outside</q> region as a face).\n"
"      The number of faces does not change no matter how you draw the graph\n"
"      (as long as you do so without the edges crossing),\n"
"      so it makes sense to ascribe the number of faces as a property of the planar graph.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_gt-planar.ptx:152
#, no-wrap
