msgid "            When you divide a multiple of 7 by 7, you get a whole number.  If you divide another number by 7, you can either write the result as a decimal or as a quotient and a remainder.  For example, <m>19 \\div 7</m> is <m>2</m> with a remainder of 5, since we can write <m>19 = 2\\cdot 7 + 5</m>.  The remainder is also called the <term>modulus</term>.  When programming in python (and many other languages), the modulus operator is written as "
