#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_counting-probability.ptx:88
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      We can get a feel for probability <em>empirically</em> by observing how frequently events occur when an experiment is repeated many times.  It often happens, as it did with the Chevalier de Mere, that our intuition about probability is not quite right.  Using the counting techniques we have studied, we can explain why our intuition is off and what the true probabilities are.\n"
