"            <m>2+3(n-1) = 3n-1</m> so the right-hand side becomes <m>4+(3n-1)n</m>.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><example><solution><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:749
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Finally, solving for <m>a_n</m> we get\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><example><solution><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:752
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
".\n"
"            Just to be sure, we check <m>a_0 = \\frac{4}{2} = 2</m>,\n"
"            <m>a_1 = \\frac{4+2}{2} = 3</m>, etc.\n"
"            We have the correct closed formula.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><title>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:762
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Summing Geometric Sequences: Multiply, Shift and\n"
"      Subtract"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:766
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        To find the sum of a geometric sequence,\n"
"        we cannot just reverse and add.\n"
"        Do you see why?\n"
"        The reason we got the same term added to itself many times is because there was a constant difference.\n"
"        So as we added that difference in one direction,\n"
"        we subtracted the difference going the other way, leaving a constant total.\n"
"        For geometric sums, we have a different technique.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><statement><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:778 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:226
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            What is <m>3 + 6 + 12 + 24 + \\cdots + 12288</m>?\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><example><solution><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:783
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Multiply each term by 2, the common ratio.\n"
"            You get <m>2S = 6 + 12 + 24 + \\cdots + 24576</m>.\n"
"            Now subtract: <m>2S - S = -3 + 24576 = 24573</m>.\n"
"            Since <m>2S - S = S</m>, we have our answer.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:792
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        To better see what happened in the above example, try writing it this way:\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:803 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>S=</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:804 source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:816
#: source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:251 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:263
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>3 \\, +</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:805 source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:811
#: source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:252 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>6 + 12 + 24 + \\cdots + 12288</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:809 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>- \\qquad 2S=</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:812 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:259
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m> + 24576</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:815 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:262
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>-S = </m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:817 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:264
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>0 + 0 + 0 +  \\cdots + 0 </m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:818 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>-24576</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:825
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Then divide both sides by <m>-1</m> and we have the same result for <m>S</m>.\n"
"        The idea is, by multiplying the sum by the common ratio,\n"
"        each term becomes the next term.\n"
"        We shift over the sum to get the subtraction to mostly cancel out,\n"
"        leaving just the first term and new last term.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><statement><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:835 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:281
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Find a closed formula for <m>S(n) = 2 + 10 + 50 + \\cdots + 2\\cdot 5^n</m>.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:840 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:286
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            The common ratio is 5.\n"
"            So we have\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:850 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:295
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>S</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:851 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:296
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>= 2 + 10 + 50 + \\cdots + 2\\cdot 5^n</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:854 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>- \\qquad 5S</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:855 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>= ~~~~~~10 + 50 + \\cdots + 2\\cdot 5^n + 2\\cdot5^{n+1}</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:858 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:303
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>-4S</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:859 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>= 2  - 2\\cdot5^{n+1}</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:866 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:310
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Thus <m>S = \\dfrac{2-2\\cdot 5^{n+1}}{-4}</m>\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:872 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:316
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Even though this might seem like a new technique,\n"
"        you have probably used it before.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><statement><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:879 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:323
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Express <m>0.464646\\ldots</m> as a fraction.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:884 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:328
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            Let <m>N = 0.46464646\\ldots</m>.\n"
"            Consider <m>0.01N</m>.\n"
"            We get:\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:895 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:338
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>N =</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:896 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:339
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>0.4646464\\ldots</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:899 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:342
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>- \\qquad 0.01N =</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:900 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:343
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>0.00464646\\ldots</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:903 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:346
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>0.99N =</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><example><solution><tabular><row><cell>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:904 source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:347
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>0.46</m>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><subsubsection><example><solution><p>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:911
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            So <m>N = \\frac{46}{99}</m>.\n"
"            What have we done?\n"
"            We viewed the repeating decimal\n"
"            <m>0.464646\\ldots</m> as a sum of the geometric sequence\n"
"            <m>0.46, 0.0046, 0.000046, \\ldots</m> The common ratio is <m>0.01</m>.\n"
"            The only real difference is that we are now computing an\n"
"            <em>infinite</em> geometric sum,\n"
"            we do not have the extra <q>last</q> term to consider.\n"
"            Really, this is the result of taking a limit as you would in calculus when you compute\n"
"            <em>infinite</em> geometric sums.\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><reading-questions><exercise><matches><match><premise>
#: source/sec_seq-arithgeom.ptx:940
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>a_n = 2n+3</m>"
msgstr ""

