#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-polynomial.ptx:279
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Generalize <xref po4a-id=0>Practice Problem 5</xref>: Find a closed formula for the sequence of differences of <m>a_n = an^2 + bn + c</m>.\n"
"        That is, prove that every quadratic sequence has arithmetic differences.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-polynomial.ptx:285
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <m>a_{n-1} = a(n-1)^2 + b(n-1) + c = an^2 - 2an + a + bn - b + c</m>.\n"
"        Therefore <m>a_n - a_{n-1} = 2an - a + b</m>, which is arithmetic.\n"
"        Notice that this is not quite the derivative of <m>a_n</m>,\n"
"        which would be <m>2an + b</m>, but it is close.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-polynomial.ptx:296
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Can you use polynomial fitting to find the formula for the <m>n</m>th term of the sequence 4, 7, 11, 18, 29, 47,\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-polynomial.ptx:297
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"?\n"
"        Explain why or why not.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-polynomial.ptx:303
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        No.\n"
"        The sequence of differences is the same as the original sequence, so no differences will be constant.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-polynomial.ptx:312
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Will the <m>n</m>th sequence of differences of <m>2, 6, 18, 54, 162, \\ldots</m> ever be constant?\n"
"        Explain.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-polynomial.ptx:318
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        No.\n"
"        The sequence is geometric, and in fact has closed formula <m>2\\cdot 3^n</m>.\n"
"        This is an exponential function,\n"
"        which is not equal to any polynomial of any degree.\n"
"        If the <m>n</m>th sequence of differences was constant,\n"
"        then the closed formula for the original sequence would be a degree <m>n</m> polynomial.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

