#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><investigation><statement><p>
#: source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          You have a large collection of <m>1\\times 1</m> squares and <m>1\\times 2</m> dominoes.\n"
"          You want to arrange these to make a <m>1 \\times 15</m> strip.\n"
"          How many ways can you do this?\n"
"         \n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><investigation><statement><p>
#: source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          What if the squares come in three different colors and the dominos come in four different colors?  And why is this second question easier than the first?\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <section><subsection><investigation><hint><p>
#: source/sec_seq-exponential.ptx:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          Start by creating a recurrence relation.  How are the different <m>1\\times 3</m> strips and <m>1 \\times 4</m> strips related to the <m>1 \\times 5</m> strips?\n"
