#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><introduction><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-strong-induction.ptx:146
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          You will prove that the Fibonacci numbers satisfy the identity <m>F_n^2 + F_{n+1}^2 = F_{2n+1}</m>.\n"
"          One way to do this is to prove the more general identity,\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><introduction><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-strong-induction.ptx:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
",\n"
"          and realize that when <m>m = n</m> we get our desired result.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><introduction><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-strong-induction.ptx:155
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          Note that we now have two variables,\n"
"          so we want to prove this for all <m>m \\ge 0</m> <em>and</em>\n"
"          all <m>n \\ge 0</m> at the same time.\n"
"          For each such pair <m>(m,n)</m>,\n"
"          let <m>P(m,n)</m> be the statement <m>F_mF_n + F_{m+1}F_{n+1} = F_{m+n+1}</m>\n"
"        "
