"              On day 2, your 2 large bunnies produce 4 mini bunnies.\n"
"              On day 3, you have 4 mini bunnies\n"
"              (produced by your 2 large bunnies)\n"
"              plus 6 large bunnies\n"
"              (your original 2 plus the 4 newly matured bunnies).\n"
"              On day 4, you will have <m>12</m> mini bunnies (2 for each of the 6 large bunnies) plus 10 large bunnies\n"
"              (your previous 6 plus the 4 newly matured).\n"
"              The sequence of total bunnies is\n"
"              <m>2, 2, 6, 10, 22, 42\\ldots</m> starting with <m>a_0 = 2</m> and <m>a_1 = 2</m>.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li>
#: source/exercises/seq-conc.ptx:237
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            <m>a_n = a_{n-1} + 2a_{n-2}</m>.\n"
"            This is because the number of bunnies is equal to the number of bunnies you had the previous day\n"
"            (both mini and large)\n"
"            plus 2 times the number you had the day before that\n"
"            (since all bunnies you had 2 days ago are now large and producing 2 new bunnies each).\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-conc.ptx:246
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Using the characteristic root technique,\n"
"              we find <m>a_n = a2^n + b(-1)^n</m>,\n"
"              and we can find <m>a</m> and <m>b</m> to give <m>a_n = \\frac{4}{3}2^n + \\frac{2}{3}(-1)^n</m>.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-conc.ptx:261
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Consider the sequence of partial sums of <em>squares</em> of Fibonacci numbers: <m>F_1^2</m>, <m>F_1^2 + F_2^2</m>, <m>F_1^2 + F_2^2 + F_3^2, \\ldots</m>.  The sequence starts <m>1, 2, 6, 15, 40,\\ldots</m> \n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-conc.ptx:265
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Guess a formula for the <m>n</m>th partial sum, in terms of Fibonacci numbers.  Hint: Write each term as a product.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-conc.ptx:270
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Prove your formula is correct by mathematical induction.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/seq-conc.ptx:275
#, no-wrap
