#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:332
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Find <m>2\\Z \\cap 3\\Z</m>. Describe the set in words, and using set\n"
"        notation. "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:337
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Express <m>\\{x \\in \\Z \\st \\exists y\\in \\Z (x = 2y \\vee x = 3y)\\}</m>\n"
"        as a union or intersection of two sets already described in this problem. "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li><p>
#: source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:348 source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:354
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              No.\n"
"            "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li>
#: source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:359
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            <m>2\\Z \\cap 3\\Z</m> is the set of all\n"
"            integers which are multiples of both 2 and 3 (so multiples of 6). Therefore <m>2\\Z \\cap 3\\Z\n"
"            = \\{x \\in \\Z \\st \\exists y\\in \\Z(x = 6y)\\}</m>. "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p><ol><li>
#: source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:363
#, no-wrap
msgid "<m>2\\Z \\cup 3\\Z</m>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:372
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Let <m>A_2</m> be the set of all multiples of 2 except for <m>2</m>. Let <m>A_3</m> be the set of all\n"
"        multiples of 3 except for 3. And so on, so that <m>A_n</m> is the set of all multiples of <m>n</m>\n"
"        except for <m>n</m>, for any <m>n \\ge 2</m>. Describe (in words) the set <m>\\bar{A_2 \\cup A_3 \\cup\n"
"          A_4 \\cup \\cdots}</m>. "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><hint><p>
#: source/exercises/intro-sets.ptx:378
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" It might help to think about what the union <m>A_2\n"
"        \\cup A_3</m> is first. Then think about what numbers are <em>not</em> in that union. What will\n"
"        happen when you also include <m>A_5</m>? "
msgstr ""

