#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><hint><p>
#: source/exercises/addtops-numbth.ptx:267
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        First reduce each number modulo 9, which can be done by adding up the digits of the numbers.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/addtops-numbth.ptx:276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        I'm thinking of a number.\n"
"        If you multiply my number by 7, add 5, and divide the result by 11,\n"
"        you will be left with a remainder of 2.\n"
"        What remainder would you get if you divided my original number by 11?\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p>
#: source/exercises/addtops-numbth.ptx:284
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        We must solve <m>7x + 5 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}</m>.\n"
"        This gives <m>x \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}</m>.\n"
"        In general, <m>x = 9 + 11k</m>,\n"
"        but when you divide any such <m>x</m> by 11, the remainder will be 9.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><statement><p>
#: source/exercises/addtops-numbth.ptx:295
#: source/exercises/addtops-numbth.ptx:316
#: source/exercises/addtops-numbth.ptx:329
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Solve the following linear Diophantine equation, using modular arithmetic (describe the general solutions).\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <exercises><exercise><solution><p>
#: source/exercises/addtops-numbth.ptx:301
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"              Divide through by 2: <m>3x + 5y = 16</m>.\n"
"              Convert to a congruence, modulo 3:\n"
"              <m>5y \\equiv 16 \\pmod 3</m>, which reduces to <m>2y \\equiv 1 \\pmod 3</m>.\n"
"              So <m>y \\equiv 2 \\pmod 3</m> or <m>y = 2 + 3k</m>.\n"
"              Plug this back into <m>3x + 5y = 16</m>, and solve for <m>x</m>,\n"
"              to get <m>x = 2-5k</m>.\n"
"              So the general solution is\n"
"              <m>x = 2-5k</m> and <m>y = 2+3k</m> for <m>k \\in \\Z</m>.\n"
"      "
msgstr ""

